{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>You shall not boil a kid.</b> From here a hint to what the Sages said: a man should not marry his fellow's wet-nurse. And this is its meaning: do not cook in the pot your fellow cooked in. Do not marry a divorcee or widow as long as the kid — the infant — needs its mother's milk, which is 24 months. And of this form we find in the chapter ערבי פסחים: 'Do not cook in the pot your fellow cooked in.' Rav Pappa said: regarding a divorcee during her husband's lifetime. If you wish, say even a widow too, because not all fingers are equal."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:43.334286829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}